    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.comment\n\n### Description\n\nI was setting up `mini.comment` and noticed that I can't seem to figure out how to do something like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal ft = require(\"Comment.ft\")\r\nft.set(\"erlang\", \"%% %s\")\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt effectively says that every time I try to comment anything in a `.erl` file use `%%` instead of `%`. I am currently using [comment](https://github.com/numToStr/Comment.nvim) plugin to do so.",
