            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "The 'mini.comment' [uses 'commentstring' option](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/085baefa6aca44526be621b15e7b688f996c2daf/doc/mini.txt#L1382-L1385) to infer what to use for commenting. Your case can be solved by setting this option locally to buffer of \"erlang\" filetype. There are two roads:\r\n\r\n- Create file 'after/ftplugin/erlang.lua' inside your Neovim config and put this line there: `vim.opt_local.commentstring = '%% %s'` (or if there is no support of `opt_local` in your Neovim version, use `vim.cmd([[setlocal commentstring=%%\\ %s]])`). I prefer this one.\r\n- Create an autocommand for `FileType` event: `vim.cmd([[au FileType erlang lua vim.opt_local.commentstring = '%% %s']])` (or use `vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd()`).",
